          "message": "support testing leaderboard models and tasks (#171)\n\nThis PR updates our use of the LM-EVAL testing to use the more recent\r\nlm-evaluation harness, and adds configuration to enable comparison of\r\nnm-vllm-ent to the HuggingFace Open LLM Leaderboard metrics. The\r\n`.github/workflows/nm-lm-eval-leaderboard.yml` workflow exercises the\r\nLeaderboard models/metrics, but has not yet been set up to run on a\r\nschedule, so it can only be triggered manually at the moment. We'll need\r\nto decide the desired schedule for this.\r\n\r\nOnly a couple of meta LLama models are included with this PR.  additional models will be added in subsequent PRs.\r\nThe ground truth metric values are obtained by setting the model ground truth to it's numbers from the Huggingface OpenLM Leaderboard, running that through the evaluation, and checking the result.  If the numbers match, we keep the ground truth.  If vllm numbers are better, we use those.  If vllm numbers are worse, the result is evaluated by research.\r\n\r\nthe `neuralmagic/lm-eval-config/models/leaderboard/HF_*.yaml` files are\r\nintended as reference to be able to use the Hugging Face backend to\r\nverify results in our environment closely match the results found at HF.",
